cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "blinkrate: measurement rules and reported electric distribution reliability"
message: "If you use these findings or this code, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andrew
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
license: MIT
keywords:
  - SAIDI
  - IEEE 1366
  - major event day
  - electric distribution reliability
  - EIA-861
abstract: >-
  IEEE 1366 permits utilities to exclude "major event days" from reported SAIDI
  using a threshold set 2.5 standard deviations up a log-normal fit to their own
  daily outage history. Using 3,427 utility-state-years of EIA-861 reliability
  filings, this work inverts the closed-form exclusion identity to show that
  re-evaluating the same filed outage records at other threshold values moves
  customer-weighted fleet SAIDI over a 6.62x range, that 30.3% of filings report
  no major event days at all (9.3x excess mass over a polynomial counterfactual),
  and that 82.9% of the 2013-2022 increase in reported SAIDI on a balanced panel
  falls in the excluded portion. The threshold sensitivity is model-implied and
  inherits IEEE 1366's own log-normality assumption; an adversarial track shows
  its direction survives heavier-tailed daily outage distributions while its
  magnitude does not.
